@ 32 - Oto-Manguean
# citation: Rensch (1977) reconstructs Proto-Oto-Manguean as having had the following phonemic inventory: Vowels could have had one of four tones, the first of which is denoted as a high tone. (From Rensch, Calvin R. (1977), “Classification of the Otomanguean Languages and the Position of Tlapanec”. Summer Institute of Linguistics Publications in Linguistics 55:53 – 108)